  "description": "Choi Jae-Won was living a carefree life abroad, surrounded by playful alphas and chasing nothing but pleasure. But when his father lures him back to Korea, he’s blindsided by a wedding—his own. The groom turns out to be Yang Joon-Hee, a childhood friend who’s grown into everything Jae-Won’s ever wanted. And before he can make sense of it, the vows are already said. Joon-Hee insists they once made a promise. Jae-Won doesn’t remember it... but something in him starts to respond anyway.\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)",
